capability lookup/path  where a program is in the folders of PATH
  heroes  process.path_of
  go      exec.LookPath, exec.ErrNotFound, exec.ErrDot, exec.Error, exec.Error.Error, exec.Error.Unwrap
  rust    -
  python  shutil.which
  note    the folders `start` reads, by the floor's rule: an empty PATH entry, or a PATH set empty, is the working folder, as POSIX's `execvp` reads it, where Go refuses a find there (`ErrDot`) and Python's `which` reads an empty PATH as no folder. A file runs where a permission bit lets someone run it; the floor also asks whether this user may (`faccessat`), which no door of `process` can ask. An empty name fails `invalid`, where Go and Python answer not found

